Code that is going away gets a document, not a comment. `{{ .Vars.prefix }}*.md` in
`{{ index .Caps "record.docs" }}/` carries `announced:`, `remove_after:` (an ISO date)
and `covers:` — the paths the deprecation applies to.

`ilk check` fails once that date has passed while the covered paths are still there,
and tells you a deprecation is finished once they are gone. `ilk deprecation list`
shows where each one stands.

A `// remove after v3` comment is invisible to everything that could act on it. Write
the document instead.
